TITLE:: PianoRoll
SUMMARY:: Piano-roll view for MIDI recording and note editing.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/PianoRollSidebar, Classes/PianoRollTimeline, Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers, Classes/SequencePlayer, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/Metronome, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter

DESCRIPTION::
LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that shows recorded notes as a piano roll. Its root LINK::Classes/View:: uses a horizontal layout: a LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: (timeline plus note canvas) and a fixed LINK::Classes/PianoRollSidebar:: on the right. It embeds LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline:: for the beat strip above the roll (left/right clicks set loop bounds; Shift+left sets playback; see LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline::). It listens for MIDI note-on and note-off events (when not in dev mode) and draws LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: entries as LINK::Classes/BorderView:: regions. LINK::#-stopRecording:: frees the recording LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s and updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes. Keyboard shortcuts are dispatched via a LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: passed in at construction.

SUBSECTION:: Keyboard editing
Focus the note area after clicking it:

TABLE::
G + digits + release    Set grid resolution to 1/N beats (N = typed integer; default 1/8)
S                       Snap selected notes to the current grid
Ctrl + Left / Right arrow      Nudge selected notes one grid step (see LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote::)
Ctrl + M                       Toggle LINK::Classes/Metronome:: on and off
1–4                     Assign part on selected notes
::

Hold G, type a denominator (for example 1 then 6 for sixteenth notes), then release G to confirm. Digits during G-hold do not assign parts. Snap and nudge apply to selected notes only; if none are selected, a brief warning is posted. Edits update the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: sequence and are allowed during playback. The metronome is toggled manually with Ctrl+M and is not started automatically when recording begins.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for embedding.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for layout.

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for colours.

ARGUMENT:: tempoClock
The LINK::Classes/TempoClock:: used for timing when recording.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When true, skips MIDI setup and fills fake notes for development.

ARGUMENT:: keyRouter
The LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: used for Record-view keyboard shortcuts.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: playLoop
Starts playback of the recorded sequence via the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer::. Returns false and posts a warning if no notes have been recorded.

METHOD:: startRecording
Arms MIDI recording (or fills fake notes in dev mode).

METHOD:: stopLoop
Stops playback via the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer::.

METHOD:: stopRecording
Stops recording, frees recording LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s, and updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes (loop bounds plus LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers#-playheadTime_:: at the loop start beat).

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyNoteEdits, prAssignPartIfSelected, prNudgeSelectedNotes, prRefreshSidebar, prRegisterKeyHandlers, prSelectedNotes, prSetGridDenominator, prSnapSelectedNotes
